00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:49,122
of the case.

291
00:06:49,162 --> 00:06:50,646
The president called it a huge victory

292
00:06:50,686 --> 00:06:51,586
anyway.

293
00:06:51,638 --> 00:06:53,122
Everything is a victory here, sir.

294
00:06:53,162 --> 00:06:53,693
Total.

295
00:06:53,733 --> 00:06:54,455
Huge.

296
00:06:54,495 --> 00:06:56,460
Nobody on this planet has ever lost.

297
00:06:56,781 --> 00:06:57,122
Sir.

298
00:06:57,162 --> 00:06:58,836
This entire report is edited.

299
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:00,364
Please have a lawyer standing by.

300
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:01,408
File twelve:

301
00:07:01,448 --> 00:07:02,650
the planet itself.

302
00:07:02,876 --> 00:07:04,269
No jokes in this one either.

303
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:06,646
A climate pattern called El Niño is

304
00:07:06,686 --> 00:07:07,979
back this year, and it may be

305
00:07:08,019 --> 00:07:10,079
one of the strongest ever recorded.

306
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,555
In Kenya, people are bracing for floods.

307
00:07:12,781 --> 00:07:14,455
This year alone, flooding there has killed

308
00:07:14,495 --> 00:07:15,888
more than sixty people.

309
00:07:16,019 --> 00:07:17,693
In Nairobi there are people living two

310
00:07:17,733 --> 00:07:18,936
meters from the river.

311
00:07:19,257 --> 00:07:19,884
One of them said:

312
00:07:19,924 --> 00:07:21,412
this water can kill us.

313
00:07:21,733 --> 00:07:23,693
And in Peru, the largest fishery in

314
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:25,031
the world has been hit.

315
00:07:25,448 --> 00:07:27,027
Events like this cost the world economy

316
00:07:27,067 --> 00:07:28,550
trillions of dollars.

317
00:07:28,590 --> 00:07:30,074
And the first to pay, sir, are

318
00:07:30,114 --> 00:07:31,698
the poorest people on the planet.

319
00:07:31,924 --> 00:07:33,888
The ones whose houses will not hold.

320
00:07:34,019 --> 00:07:35,027
File thirteen:

321
00:07:35,067 --> 00:07:35,967
culture.

322
00:07:36,114 --> 00:07:37,693
The Booker Prize, one of their highest

323
00:07:37,733 --> 00:07:39,122
honors for a book, went to a

324
00:07:39,162 --> 00:07:41,312
novel about the world after it ends.

325
00:07:41,352 --> 00:07:43,317
It is called The End of Everything.

326
00:07:43,543 --> 00:07:44,836
The author is the oldest winner the

327
00:07:44,876 --> 00:07:46,079
prize has ever had.

328
00:07:46,305 --> 00:07:47,598
And the book has been described as:

329
00:07:47,638 --> 00:07:48,936
baffling, but brilliant.

330
00:07:49,257 --> 00:07:50,550
Much like this planet, sir.

331
00:07:50,590 --> 00:07:51,490
Baffling.

332
00:07:51,543 --> 00:07:52,555
Without the second part.

333
00:07:53,067 --> 00:07:54,269
Even they can see it coming.

334
00:07:54,590 --> 00:07:55,698
They just give it awards.

335
00:07:56,114 --> 00:07:56,741
And the last file:

336
00:07:56,781 --> 00:07:57,681
commerce.

337
00:07:57,733 --> 00:07:59,979
Skims, the company owned by Kim Kardashian,

338
00:08:00,019 --> 00:08:02,741
sold a holiday advent calendar for a

339
00:08:02,781 --> 00:08:03,217
hundred and forty-eight dollars.

340
00:08:03,257 --> 00:08:03,979
Inside:

341
00:08:04,019 --> 00:08:04,919
hair clips.

342
00:08:04,971 --> 00:08:05,888
And keychains.

343
00:08:06,114 --> 00:08:07,217
Customers said it looked like what you

344
00:08:07,257 --> 00:08:08,460
find behind the sofa.

345
00:08:08,781 --> 00:08:10,364
The company is now offering refunds.

346
00:08:10,590 --> 00:08:12,265
That company is valued at five billion

347
00:08:12,305 --> 00:08:13,122
dollars.

348
00:08:13,162 --> 00:08:14,455
One customer said the box looked like

349
00:08:14,495 --> 00:08:16,269
things her cat collects around the house.

350
00:08:16,590 --> 00:08:17,884
And its owner is one of California's

351
00:08:17,924 --> 00:08:19,221
two hundred billionaires.

352
00:08:19,733 --> 00:08:20,931
The ones the voters just protected from

353
00:08:20,971 --> 00:08:21,884
a tax.

354
00:08:21,924 --> 00:08:23,412
Final assessment, sir.

355
00:08:23,543 --> 00:08:25,698
They negotiate and never agree.

356
00:08:25,829 --> 00:08:27,408
They vote against themselves.

357
00:08:27,448 --> 00:08:28,741
And they give prizes to the end

358
00:08:28,781 --> 00:08:29,681
of the world.

359
00:08:29,829 --> 00:08:31,789
And among them are civilians paying for

360
00:08:31,829 --> 00:08:33,317
wars they never chose.

361
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:34,931
That, sir, is the one thing on

362
00:08:34,971 --> 00:08:36,555
this planet that is not funny.

363
00:08:37,067 --> 00:08:37,983
Recommendation:

364
00:08:38,114 --> 00:08:39,217
do not intervene.

365
00:08:39,257 --> 00:08:40,745
They are getting there on their own.

366
00:08:41,257 --> 00:08:42,265
One last note.

367
00:08:42,305 --> 00:08:43,793
Not one of them has noticed me.

368
00:08:44,114 --> 00:08:45,014
They are busy.

369
00:08:45,257 --> 00:08:46,741
This has been the Earth Report.

370
00:08:46,781 --> 00:08:47,598
Agent Peek.

371
00:08:47,638 --> 00:08:48,650
End of transmission.
